<details>
<summary><strong>Shell - wscat</strong></summary>

```bash
# wscat speaks raw WebSocket — connect, then type the STOMP frames yourself,
# each terminated by a NUL byte (Ctrl-@ / \0 on most terminals).
npx wscat -c '{{url}}'

# Once connected, send the CONNECT frame:
CONNECT
accept-version:{{stompVersion}}
host:{{host}}
{{#each connectHeaders}}{{key}}:{{value}}
{{/each}}

^@
{{#each subscriptions}}
# Subscribe to {{destination}}:
SUBSCRIBE
id:{{id}}
destination:{{destination}}
ack:{{ackMode}}

^@
{{/each}}
{{#if sendDestination}}
# Send a message to {{sendDestination}}:
SEND
destination:{{sendDestination}}
{{#each sendHeaders}}{{key}}:{{value}}
{{/each}}

{{sendBody}}
^@
{{/if}}
# Disconnect:
DISCONNECT

^@
```

</details>
